Laelia grows every time a card leaves your library or graveyard for exile, and she makes some of that exile herself when she attacks. So every impulse-draw spell in this deck is two things at once: a card you can play this turn, and a +1/+1 counter on a hasty commander. Attack every turn, play what she flips, and let Kediss copy her damage to the whole table.

# The commander
Laelia, the Blade Reforged :: three mana, haste. Whenever she attacks, exile the top card of your library; you may play it this turn. Whenever ONE OR MORE cards are put into exile from your library and/or graveyard, put a +1/+1 counter on her.
"One or more" means one counter per exile EVENT, not per card. Light Up the Stage exiling two cards is one counter; three separate exile effects are three counters. Cheap, repeated exile beats one big exile.
She only counts exile from YOUR library and graveyard. Ragavan and Tibalt's Trickery exile from opponents' libraries and do not grow her.

# Key pairs
Laelia, the Blade Reforged + Kediss, Emberclaw Familiar :: whenever your commander deals combat damage to an opponent, Kediss deals that much damage to each other opponent. A 10-power Laelia connecting once is 30 damage across the table.
Laelia, the Blade Reforged + Temur Battle Rage :: double strike, and trample once she has 4 power. Two hits means two Kediss triggers.
Laelia, the Blade Reforged + Chandra's Ignition :: she deals damage equal to her power to each other creature and each opponent. With 15 power that is 15 to everyone and a cleared board.
Underworld Breach + Grim Lavamancer :: both exile cards from your graveyard as a cost, and every escape and every Lavamancer shot is a counter on Laelia.
Underworld Breach + Wheel of Fortune + Jeska's Will :: the big turn. Wheel gives every opponent seven cards, so Jeska's Will makes seven red mana; escape Wheel again from the graveyard (its {2}{R} plus three other cards exiled) and do it again. Each loop refills everyone, makes mana, and puts a counter on Laelia. A three-card line, so it fits Bracket 3; save it for a turn that ends the game.

# Exile engines — every one is a counter
Outpost Siege :: choose Khans: exile your top card every upkeep and play it this turn. A counter every turn, before combat.
Tavern Brawler :: a Background your commander picks up: exile your top card every upkeep, and she gets +X/+0 equal to its mana value.
Bonehoard Dracosaur :: exiles your top two every upkeep, and makes a Treasure or a Dinosaur depending on what they were.
Urabrask, Heretic Praetor :: exiles your top card every upkeep; you may play it.
Valakut Exploration :: every land you play exiles the top card for you to play.
Chandra, Torch of Defiance :: +1 exiles your top card to cast, or deals 2 to each opponent.
Light Up the Stage :: two cards for one or three mana.
Reckless Impulse :: two cards.
Wrenn's Resolve :: two cards.
Glimpse the Impossible :: three cards this turn.
Jeska's Will :: with Laelia out, both modes: mana from an opponent's hand AND exile your top three to play.
Professional Face-Breaker :: combat damage makes Treasure; sacrifice Treasure to exile and play your top card.
Party Thrasher :: discard a card in your first main phase to exile your top two and play one of them this turn. Noncreature spells you cast from exile also gain convoke.
Tectonic Giant :: when it attacks, deal 3 to each opponent or exile your top two to play.
Etali, Primal Storm :: when it attacks, exile the top card of every library and cast them free.
Plargg and Nassari :: each upkeep, every player exiles cards down to a nonland card. An opponent vetoes one, and you cast up to two of the others free.
Trumpeting Carnosaur :: discover 5 on entering.
Geological Appraiser :: discover 3 when cast.
Etali's Favor :: an Aura that discovers 3 and gives trample.
Hidden Volcano :: a land that discovers 4.
Throes of Chaos :: cascade, then retrace it from your graveyard by discarding a land: cascade again.
Wild-Magic Sorcerer :: the first spell you cast from exile each turn cascades.
Spinerock Knoll :: hideaway exiles four cards when it enters; play the hidden one free once an opponent took 7 damage this turn.
Grim Lavamancer :: exile two cards from your graveyard for 2 damage. A counter every time.
Mines of Moria :: exile three cards from your graveyard for two Treasures.
Underworld Breach :: every nonland card in your graveyard gains escape, paid partly by exiling three other cards. Each escape is a counter.

# Making each hit count
Kediss, Emberclaw Familiar :: the reason one big hit kills three players.
Commander's Plate :: +3/+3 and protection from every colour outside red, for {3} on your commander.
Shadowspear :: trample and lifelink, and it strips hexproof and indestructible from their blockers.
The Reaver Cleaver :: trample, and a Treasure for each point of combat damage to a player.
Sword of Feast and Famine :: protection from black and green; on a hit, they discard and you untap all your lands for a second main phase.
Inti, Seneschal of the Sun :: whenever you attack, discard a card to put a counter and trample on an attacker; whenever you discard, exile your top card to play.
Passionate Archaeologist :: a Background: every spell you cast from exile deals its mana value to an opponent.
Temur Battle Rage :: double strike.
Rogue's Passage :: {4}: she can't be blocked.
Shinka, the Bloodsoaked Keep :: first strike for a legendary attacker.
Delayed Blast Fireball :: 2 to each opponent and their creatures, or 5 if cast from exile. Foretell it (exile it face down from your hand for {2}; that exile is from your hand, so no counter) or flip it off Laelia's attack.

# Playing the cards you exiled
Birgi, God of Storytelling :: {R} for every spell you cast, kept all turn. A turn of exiled cards pays for itself.
Ruby Medallion :: red spells cost {1} less.
Runaway Steam-Kin :: grows on red spells and cashes in for {R}{R}{R}.
Neheb, the Eternal :: after combat, {R} for each point of life your opponents lost this turn. A big Laelia swing refunds a whole second main phase.
Mana Geyser :: {R} for each tapped land your opponents control.
Pyretic Ritual :: {R}{R}{R} for two.
Seething Song :: {R}{R}{R}{R}{R} for three.
Simian Spirit Guide :: a free {R} from your hand.
Wheel of Fortune :: everyone discards and draws seven. Your discards feed Breach and Lavamancer.
Unexpected Windfall :: two cards and two Treasures.
The One Ring :: protection for a turn cycle, then a card every upkeep.

# Keeping her swinging
Lightning Greaves :: haste and shroud, equips for {0}. Move it off before casting your own targeted spells on her.
Swiftfoot Boots :: hexproof keeps your own spells legal.
Mithril Coat :: flash, attaches for free on entering: indestructible.
The Ozolith :: if she leaves the battlefield, her counters move to The Ozolith, then onto a creature at your next combat. Recast her and they come home.
Command Beacon :: put her back into your hand without paying commander tax.
Deflecting Swat :: free while she is out: redirect the removal aimed at her.
Bolt Bend :: costs {R} once she has 4 power: redirect a single-target spell.
Untimely Malfunction :: redirect, destroy an artifact, or stop two blockers.
Tibalt's Trickery :: counter anything; its controller mills a few and casts a random replacement.

# Answers
Lightning Bolt :: 3 damage for one mana.
Abrade :: 3 to a creature or destroy an artifact.
Chaos Warp :: shuffle away any permanent.
Vandalblast :: one artifact, or all of theirs for five.
Blasphemous Act :: 13 to every creature, usually for one or two mana. Laelia's counters come back via The Ozolith.
Chandra's Ignition :: a one-sided wipe that also hits every opponent.
Grim Lavamancer :: repeatable 2 damage.

# Mana
Sol Ring :: the usual.
Arcane Signet :: the usual.
Mind Stone :: a rock that cashes in for a card.
Lotus Petal :: a free mana for a turn-two Laelia.
Arena of Glory :: exert for {R}{R} that gives a creature haste.
Nykthos, Shrine to Nyx :: red mana equal to your devotion.
Valakut, the Molten Pinnacle :: with six Mountains out, each new Mountain deals 3.
War Room :: pay 1 life and {3} for a card.
Urza's Saga :: fetches Sol Ring, Lotus Petal, The Ozolith or Shadowspear at chapter III.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep Laelia's mana, a land, and one cheap exile spell or piece of equipment. Turn two or three Laelia, attack immediately, and play whatever she flips.
Lay out an upkeep exile engine (Outpost Siege, Tavern Brawler, Bonehoard Dracosaur, Urabrask) early: they grow her every turn before she even attacks.
Get Kediss down before the big swing, and hold Deflecting Swat for the removal.
